From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joinery Build <build@joinery.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:55:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): switch between Joinery's layout and classic
 Godot

Joinery-only, not meant for upstream: it guards the layout changes that
earlier Joinery patches make.

One editor setting, interface/joinery/editor_layout (Joinery or Classic
Godot), read once at startup, decides the layout. Classic turns every
layout change off: Scene, FileSystem, Import, History, Inspector,
Signals and Groups default to their stock slots, the 2D/3D/Script
buttons return to the title bar, the run bar shows all its buttons, the
bottom panel keeps its overflow arrows, dock menu and status strip, and
there is no navigation column for the tool rail. The theme presets are
not part of the layout and stay as chosen.

Each layout keeps its own dock arrangement in editor_layout.cfg
(docks_joinery, docks_classic, and joinery_view naming the last one), so
switching opens the other layout as it was left, or at its default the
first time. A layout saved by stock Godot still migrates once into
Joinery's.

Editor > "Switch to classic Godot view" (or "Switch to Joinery view"),
also in the command palette, asks first and offers Restart or "On next
start"; the setting is marked restart-if-changed for Editor Settings.
